scanner: never lose a deferred start-condition pop, never pop an empty stack

scanner_pop_start_cond() keeps a count of deferred pops (flex_state_pop)
for close_scope events that arrive while the scanner has already moved
into a nested start condition (bison lookahead).  Two defects in the
drain logic:

1. When draining stops early because the newly exposed start condition is
   still active, the CURRENT call's own pop is silently dropped instead of
   being re-queued.  Each occurrence desynchronizes the pop accounting
   from the real flex start-condition stack (observed on the standard fw4
   ruleset at "meta nfproto ipv4 meta l4proto igmp counter accept": the
   counter scope's pop is lost).

2. yy_top_state()/yy_pop_state() are called without checking that the
   start-condition stack is non-empty.  Once the bookkeeping is off (see
   above and the IGMP grammar leak fixed in the previous patch),
   yy_top_state() reads stack[-1] (UB) and yy_pop_state() hits the fatal
   "start-condition stack underflow" flex error, aborting the whole parse.
   This is what made the fw4-rendered ruleset unloadable on the ONU
   (firewall/NAT completely absent).

Re-queue the own pop on early drain exit, and guard both pop sites so a
residual imbalance degrades into a no-op instead of a fatal error.

--- a/src/scanner.l
+++ b/src/scanner.l
@@ -1350,6 +1350,11 @@
 	yy_push_state((int)type, scanner);
 }
 
+static bool scanner_start_stack_empty(void *scanner)
+{
+	return ((struct yyguts_t *)scanner)->yy_start_stack_ptr <= 0;
+}
+
 void scanner_pop_start_cond(void *scanner, enum startcond_type t)
 {
 	struct parser_state *state = yyget_extra(scanner);
@@ -1363,14 +1368,22 @@
 
 	while (state->flex_state_pop) {
 		state->flex_state_pop--;
+		if (scanner_start_stack_empty(scanner))
+			return;
 		state->startcond_type = yy_top_state(scanner);
 		yy_pop_state(scanner);
 
 		t = state->startcond_type;
-		if (state->startcond_active[t])
+		if (state->startcond_active[t]) {
+			/* defer our own pop, else it is lost */
+			state->flex_state_pop++;
 			return;
+		}
 	}
 
+	if (scanner_start_stack_empty(scanner))
+		return;
+
 	state->startcond_type = yy_top_state(scanner);
 
 	yy_pop_state(scanner);
